\title{Bayesian Stable Isotope Mixing Models using Stan}
\description{
\code{bsimms} fits Bayesian stable isotope mixing models (SIMMs) via
\href{https://mc-stan.org}{Stan}, estimating the proportional contribution of
two or more sources to a mixture from tracer data such as stable
isotopes.
}
\details{
\code{bsimms} generates a bespoke Stan program from a user-supplied model
specification and fits it via MCMC, using either the \code{cmdstanr} or
\code{rstan} package as backend. It supports the core modelling options of
the JAGS-based package \code{MixSIAR} (raw or summarised source and trophic
discrimination factor data, concentration dependence, flexible error
structures, cross-tracer covariance) and extends them by letting source
proportions depend on an arbitrary \code{lme4}-style fixed- and random-effects
formula of mixture-level covariates, with weakly informative, data-scaled
default priors that can be fully overridden. Source proportions are
modelled in isometric log-ratio (ILR) coordinates, so that an
unconstrained linear predictor maps onto the source simplex via a
numerically stable softmax transform.

